  "overview": {
    "full": "Border Gateway Protocol",
    "description": "The internet is a network of networks: tens of thousands of them, run by internet providers, clouds, universities and companies, each with its own AS number. BGP is how their border routers tell each other which addresses they can reach. Every router passes on what it learns with its own number added, so each network builds its own map of the paths to every address on the internet.",
