  "outro": {
    "title": "Route learned",
    "desc": "Announced, passed on, used",
    "text": "The hosting network announced its addresses, the transit network passed them on with its own number added, and the ISP’s router used that path for the laptop’s packets. When the route was withdrawn, the news spread the same way. There is no central map: every network builds its own from what its neighbours say. Press REPLAY to watch it again.",
