    {
      "title": "Many Networks",
      "desc": "Each with its own number",
      "detail": "The internet is more than 75,000 separate networks, called autonomous systems (ASes): internet providers, clouds, universities, big companies, each with a number. Here are three: the laptop’s ISP (AS 64500), a transit network that carries others’ traffic (AS 64510), and the hosting network of www.example.com (AS 64511). BGP is how their routers tell each other where every address can be reached.",
