    {
      "title": "Open a Session",
      "desc": "TCP to port 179",
      "detail": "BGP routers don’t discover each other: engineers at both ends set each other up as neighbours. The ISP’s router opens a TCP connection to the transit router on port 179. They are directly connected, so their packets go out with a TTL of 1: they can’t cross even one more router, so the session only works between direct neighbours.",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Port",
          "TCP 179"
        ],
        [
          "Neighbours",
          "Set up by hand"
        ],
        [
          "TTL",
          "1: the next router only"
        ]
      ],
