    {
      "title": "Passed On",
      "desc": "Each network adds its number",
      "detail": "The transit router accepts the route and passes it to its other neighbours, the ISP among them, with its own number added to the front: AS_PATH 64510 64511, and itself as the next hop. The ISP’s router may hear of the same prefix from several neighbours. It picks one by its own policy first (routes through paying customers before others, say), then by the shortest AS path.",
