      "desc": "Packets go where BGP said",
      "detail": "When the laptop connects to www.example.com (its address found by DNS as usual), its packets reach the ISP, whose router now sends anything for 203.0.113.0/24 to the transit router, and the transit router sends it on to the hosting network. The answer comes back by whatever route the hosting network chose towards the laptop’s ISP: on the internet the way back is often different from the way there.",
