    {
      "title": "Withdrawn",
      "desc": "Routes can be taken back",
      "detail": "Later the hosting network takes the prefix back, as it would if a link failed: an UPDATE listing it under withdrawn routes. The transit router passes it on, and within seconds to minutes networks everywhere forget the path. A session that goes quiet past its hold time loses all its routes at once. In 2021 Facebook withdrew the routes to its own DNS servers and vanished from the internet for six hours.",
